# SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-TUR-Noncommercial-1.0.0
#
# What a TUR desktop program may import, link and write, and what it must
# not. The data of the licence boundary check, desktop/ci/boundary.py, which
# the `boundary` job of the desktop workflow runs on every change.
#
# Sources: AGENTS.md, "Licence boundary rules"; docs/architecture/
# desktop-experience.md, sections 3.5, 4 and 5.1; ADR-0016.
#
# TUR's programs carry the project's noncommercial licence. Such a program may
# link, dynamically, a library under the LGPL. It may not link or import
# anything that is GPL-only: that would make the combined program GPL. Adding
# an `allow` line means its licence was checked file by file where a project
# mixes licences. Removing or weakening a `forbid` line needs an ADR.
#
# Rules, one to a line; "#" starts a comment. NAME and PATHS are globs
# ("*" matches anything, including "/" and "."). PATHS is a comma-separated
# list of repository paths; a leading "!" takes paths away again.
#
#   allow  KIND  NAME  PATHS  LICENCE         permitted, in the files PATHS matches
#   forbid KIND  NAME  REASON...              never permitted; checked before `allow`
#   literals PATHS                            QML files that may contain colour literals
#   deny-text PATHS  REGEX  REASON...         text that must not occur in those files
#
#   KIND   qml      a QML module, as written after "import"
#          cmake    a CMake package or target: KF6Kirigami, Qt6::Quick. A
#                   component of find_package(Qt6 COMPONENTS X) is Qt6::X
#          include  a C++ header, as written between < > or " "
#          word     an identifier in C++ source
#          soname   a shared library a built program or library needs
#
# Anything not allowed is refused, so that a new dependency is always a
# visible change to this file.

